<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Exhibition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1851</span> · Also known as Great Exhibition of the Works of Industry of All Nations</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Exhibition of the Works of Industry of All Nations was an international exhibition held in the Crystal Palace in Hyde Park, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, from May to October 1851. Organised by Prince Albert and Henry Cole, it displayed manufactures and inventions from around the world, attracted about six million visitors and showcased <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s industrial leadership.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-exhibition.jpg" alt="Great Exhibition" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Read &amp;amp; Co. Engravers &amp;amp; Printers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Crystal_Palace_in_Hyde_Park_for_Grand_International_Exhibition_of_1851.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
